<!--
  <summary>
  Stats screen (custom window 1153): JellyStat's viewing figures as a page.
  </summary>
  <remarks>
  Everything on this page is read from the JellyStat.* Home window
  properties that script.jellystat (0.26.5 or later) publishes from its
  own service every five minutes: this month and all time from the
  library, the last seven days from its play log. The skin computes nothing
  and reads no database, so the page needs only the add-on to be running.

  It is reached from the main menu entry and the corner icon on Home, both
  of which exist only while script.jellystat is installed, so a box without
  it never sees this page and is never told about it. With the add-on
  installed but not yet reporting (the first minute or two after Kodi
  starts, or a box that has not read its library) the tiles give way to a
  single line saying so, which is the nearest thing to a prompt this page
  ever shows.

  The seven daily bars are a static list: a progress control can take its
  percentage from a list item property but not from a window property, so
  each day rides on an item with its share of the busiest day as "pct".
  </remarks>
-->
